      "message": "Agree with Ted\u0027s PS1 comment and glad it\u0027s fixed: with the envelope now derived from headers this line is load-bearing. Verified: getaddresses([\u0027a@example.com@b@example.com\u0027]) -\u003e [(\u0027\u0027, \u0027\u0027)] (no valid address), while \u0027, \u0027.join parses both recipients. For reference, 2.2.6\u0027s \u0027@\u0027.join worked only because Postman composed a single user@domain address; here recipients are full addresses, so the comma join is the right call. The two-recipient case in the new test covers this.",
