      "side": 1,
      "message": "Root cause confirmed. With to_addrs given, smtplib overrides the header-derived envelope; only when to_addrs is None does send_message build the envelope from getaddresses([To, Bcc, Cc]) (verified in CPython 3 smtplib source) - so the Cc header was present but no RCPT TO was issued for it, and report_cc admins silently received nothing. This restores 2.2.6 postman.py, which called send_message(msg) with a comma-joined Cc header.\n\nRecommended follow-up this change exposes: two callers pass bare usernames as Cc - plugins/builtin/validators/environment.py sends report_cc.split(\u0027,\u0027) unqualified, and tools/jira_watchers.py sends cc\u003d[submitter] (while qualifying the To recipient with @domain). getaddresses treats \u0027admin1\u0027 as an address, so the envelope will now attempt RCPT TO:\u003cadmin1\u003e - MTA-dependent mis-delivery or refusal. Note partial refusal does not fail the send (SMTPRecipientsRefused is only raised when ALL recipients are refused), so worst case stays the silent drop. Please qualify those with @domain like notify.py/notify_tenant.py do.",
      "revId": "07b64c5547ed88b4aaeb5e6f5f73ea8f1b50cc8f",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
